    "notationLabel": "Clairnote DN — reproduction study",
    "notationFootnote": "",
    "author": "Paul Morris",
    "description": "Reproduction study — inspired by Clairnote DN (Paul Morris, 2006). Major-third 2-line staff at E/G# with a C ledger; binary-6-6 fill — the line-side whole-tone set {C,D,E,F#,G#,A#} solid, the other set hollow (per the operator reference). Clairnote's own key signatures (session 55): a dot for each note of the key, taking the noteheads' fill, in stacks that change at each change of odd and even, a tail up on each flat and down on each sharp, the tails imported as filled shapes. The vertical compression, the custom clef (E1, form not shown → omitted), the double-stem half notes (E3) and alternative accidental signs (E4) are unimplemented/omitted — documented deviations. Design CC BY-SA 4.0; no code ported from clairnote.ly. Built from the public gallery description/image; not endorsed by or derived from the original.",
    "systemName": "Clairnote DN",
    "systemCreator": "Paul Morris",
    "systemYear": 2006,
    "sourceUrl": "https://musicnotation.org/system/clairnote-dn-by-paul-morris/",
